# Build output. `./scripts/package.sh` writes function.<YYYYMMDD>.zip
# here -- ~3.9 MB, and fully determined by package-lock.json plus src/, so
# committing it would be storing a derived binary that goes stale the moment
# either changes.
#
# This file ignores everything except itself, which is what makes the directory
# exist in a fresh clone rather than being conjured by Docker on first use.
#
# The root .gitignore deliberately does NOT list dist/. Git never descends into
# an ignored directory, so a parent-level rule would make this file untrackable
# and defeat the point. If you ever add `dist/` up there, this stops working and
# nothing warns you.
*
!.gitignore
